            <div xml:id="d456">

                <pb facs="0566" n="498" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg498"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72/2327½a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the German Ambassador</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bernstorff</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-15">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 15, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I have been hoping to
                    hear from you in regard to the <hi rendition="#italic">Lusitania</hi> affair. I
                    feel that continued delay in reaching an agreement in this matter may
                    precipitate a situation which both of us would seriously regret. I trust that
                    you can give me an indication as to the attitude of your Government upon the
                    formula which we considered sometime ago.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
